    "notes": "AfroLID v1.5 (UBC-NLP), an XLM-R classifier over 517 African languages; its ISO 639-3 labels are reported as BCP-47 tags. Upstream behaviour, reproduced with the unmodified PyTorch checkpoint: short Yoruba sentences can come out as Wolof or Fula with a top-1 probability under 0.4 (1 of 8 FLORES-200 devtest Yoruba sentences, 'O ko ago ilekun WiFi, O wi.'). Longer Yoruba is classified yor with or without tone marks. Text in a language outside the 517 still gets an African label, at times with a probability over 0.9 (English, French, Portuguese and Chinese FLORES-200 sentences); the model's nan_lang label did not fire for any of them.",
